# COPY - Copy files

To keep the original file in A0 and make a copy in D0:

```
COPY A0:README.TXT D0:
```

Resident COPY refuses to replace an existing destination unless you give
`/O`. Keep a separate copy of important data before replacing a file.

For verified copies, use the transient command, for example
`:COPY A0:README.TXT D0: /V`. For destination-first syntax, see
[PIP syntax](PIP.HLP#syntax). To copy from several user areas, see
[PIP selectors](PIP.HLP#selectors).
